    <section id="what-is">
      <h2>What is Female Fertility Hormone Testing?</h2>
      <p>Female fertility hormone testing is a specialized diagnostic blood panel that measures ovarian egg reserve, pituitary gland signaling, ovulation timing, and metabolic hormone balance. Essential blood tests include Anti-Müllerian Hormone (AMH) for egg count, Cycle Day 2/3 FSH, LH, and Estradiol for baseline follicle development, Cycle Day 21 Progesterone for ovulation verification, and TSH, Prolactin, and Fasting Insulin for endocrine and PCOS screening. In Lahore, comprehensive female fertility hormone testing provides immediate diagnostic clarity for irregular menstrual cycles, polycystic ovaries, unexplained subfertility, and age-related fertility planning, guiding personalized treatment pathways such as Letrozole Ovulation Induction, IUI, or IVF/ICSI.</p>
      <div class="callout"><b>In simple words.</b> Hormones are chemical messengers that control your cycle. A few blood tests, taken on the right days, show how many eggs you have left, whether you ovulate, and whether your thyroid or sugar balance is getting in the way. It is a fast, low-risk first step.</div>
    </section>

    <section id="why-it-matters">
      <h2>Why Female Fertility Hormone Testing Matters</h2>
      <p>Hormones serve as the biochemical master switches regulating every phase of female reproductive health, from initial ovarian follicle recruitment and oocyte maturation to ovulation timing, luteal phase adequacy, and uterine lining receptivity. When subtle hormonal imbalances occur, women may experience irregular menstrual cycles, anovulation, poor egg quality, or recurrent early pregnancy loss.</p>
      <p>At Kamran Fertility Clinic, under the expert clinical direction of Dr. Kamran Saleem, female fertility hormone testing is conducted with strict evidence-based precision. Moving away from outdated, vague laboratory labels like "hormonal analysis," our diagnostic framework utilizes exact-match, high-utility blood profiles designed to answer four fundamental clinical questions:</p>
      <div class="cards" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)">
