      <h3 id="h-amh">A. Anti-Müllerian Hormone (AMH): The Gold-Standard Ovarian Reserve Marker</h3>
      <p>Anti-Müllerian Hormone is a glycoprotein secreted by small pre-antral and primary antral follicles within the ovaries. Because AMH production remains relatively constant throughout the menstrual cycle, blood sampling can be performed on any day of the month, independent of menstrual bleeding.</p>
      <p><b>Clinical Significance:</b> AMH reflects the quantitative pool of remaining oocytes (egg reserve). It serves as the single most reliable predictor of reproductive lifespan and ovarian response to stimulation medications during IVF and ICSI cycles.</p>
      <div class="callout"><b>In simple words.</b> AMH estimates how many eggs you have left. It shows egg quantity, not egg quality, and a single number cannot predict pregnancy on its own.</div>
      <p><b>AMH Diagnostic Reference Table:</b></p>
      <div class="tw"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>AMH Level (ng/mL)</th><th>Ovarian Reserve Classification</th><th>Clinical Interpretation &amp; Recommended Treatment Pathway</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{amh.map(r => <tr><th scope="row">{r[0]}</th><td>{r[1]}</td><td>{r[2]}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3 id="h-basal" style="margin-top:34px">B. Basal Menstrual Cycle Profile (Cycle Day 2 or Day 3)</h3>
      <p>Basal hormone testing must be performed strictly on Cycle Day 2 or Day 3 (where Day 1 represents the first day of full menstrual flow). Drawing blood during this basal window provides an unmasked baseline of pituitary-ovarian communication:</p>
      <div class="cols">
        {basal.map(([h, p, s]) => <div class="card"><h3>{h}</h3><p>{p}</p><p style="margin-top:10px;color:var(--c-primary);font-weight:600">{s}</p></div>)}
      </div>

      <h3 id="h-d21" style="margin-top:34px">C. Mid-Luteal Ovulation Verification Profile (Cycle Day 21)</h3>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:14px">
        <p><b>Serum Progesterone:</b> Tested 7 days prior to expected menses (Cycle Day 21 in a standard 28-day cycle, or adjusted for longer cycles).</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px"><b>Clinical Significance:</b> Progesterone is produced by the corpus luteum following ovulation. A Day 21 Progesterone level > 10 to 15 ng/mL confirms robust ovulation and adequate luteal phase support to maintain early embryo implantation. Levels below 5 ng/mL indicate anovulation or luteal phase deficiency requiring targeted progesterone supplementation.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;color:var(--c-primary);font-weight:600">In simple words: progesterone rises after you ovulate. A good level shows an egg was released and the lining is supported. See also <a href="/services/assessment/ovulation-assessment">ovulation assessment</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <h3 id="h-endocrine" style="margin-top:34px">D. Endocrine &amp; Metabolic Screening Panel</h3>
      <p>Reproductive performance is deeply interconnected with systemic thyroid and metabolic function. Dr. Kamran Saleem evaluates three critical non-ovarian hormones:</p>
      <div class="cards">
        {endo.map(([h, p, s]) => <div class="card"><h3>{h}</h3><p>{p}</p><p style="margin-top:10px;color:var(--c-primary);font-weight:600">{s}</p></div>)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="timing">
      <h2>Precise Timing &amp; Patient Preparation Master Matrix</h2>
      <p>Accurate diagnostic results depend strictly on correct cycle timing and proper laboratory preparation. Use this reference guide prior to your visit:</p>
      <div class="tw"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Hormone Test</th><th>Required Menstrual Cycle Timing</th><th>Fasting / Patient Preparation Instructions</th><th>Primary Diagnostic Objective</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{timing.map(r => <tr><th scope="row">{r[0]}</th><td>{r[1]}</td><td>{r[2]}</td><td>{r[3]}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table></div>
    </section>

    <section id="reference">
      <h2>Quick Reference: What the Numbers Usually Mean</h2>
      <p>This summary uses the same values Dr. Kamran applies in the sections above. Your own result is always read together with your age, cycle and scans.</p>
      <div class="tw"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Test</th><th>Usual healthy value</th><th>May need attention</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{reference.map(r => <tr><th scope="row">{r[0]}</th><td>{r[1]}</td><td>{r[2]}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table></div>
    </section>

    <section id="interpretation">
      <h2>Diagnostic Interpretation &amp; Treatment Decision Pathways</h2>
      <p>Once your blood results are processed in our certified Lahore laboratory, Dr. Kamran Saleem conducts an unhurried consultation to translate raw numbers into a clear, personalized medical roadmap:</p>
      <div class="cols">
        {pathways.map(([h, d, a, i]) => <div class="card"><span class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" set:html={icons[i]} /></span><h3>{h}</h3><p><b>Diagnosis:</b> {d}</p><p style="margin-top:8px"><b>Action Plan:</b> <span set:html={a} /></p></div>)}
      </div>
      <p class="note">Hormone results are one part of the picture. A pelvic ultrasound, a tubal check where indicated and your partner's <a href="/services/assessment/semen-analysis">semen analysis</a> complete it, as described in the <a href="/services/assessment/female-fertility-assessment">Female Fertility Assessment</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="test-day">
      <h2>What Happens on Test Day</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        {steps.map((s, i) => (
          <li class="step" id={`step-${i + 1}`}>
            <div class="media"><span class="ph"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" set:html={icons[s.icon]} /></span></div>
            <div class="body"><span class="num">Step {i + 1} · {s.time}</span><h3>{s.t}</h3><p>{s.d}</p></div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="pricing">
      <h2>Transparent Pricing Guidelines &amp; Fast Report Turnaround in Lahore</h2>
      <p>At Kamran Fertility Clinic, we believe in complete financial transparency prior to any diagnostic work:</p>
      <div class="cards">
        <div class="card"><h3>Individual Test Rates</h3><p>Standardized, affordable pricing for single blood tests (such as standalone AMH or Day 2/3 basal profiles).</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Bundled Female Fertility Hormone Package</h3><p>Cost-effective comprehensive packages covering AMH, FSH, LH, Estradiol, Prolactin, TSH, and Progesterone.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Fast 24-Hour Turnaround</h3><p>AMH and endocrine results are delivered within 24 hours via encrypted digital reports or direct clinic dispatch for seamless review during your consultation.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="next-steps">
      <h2>After Your Hormone Test: Related Services</h2>
      <p>Your results decide the next step. These pages explain the tests and treatments that most often follow.</p>
      <div class="cards">
        {treatments.map(([n, h, d]) => <a class="card link" href={h}><h3>{n}</h3><p>{d}</p></a>)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="faq">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      {faqs.map(([q, a]) => <details><summary>{q}</summary><p>{a}</p></details>)}
    </section>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="cta" id="locations"><div class="w">
  <h2>Schedule Your Unhurried Consultation with Dr. Kamran Saleem</h2>
  <p>Accurate hormone testing is the essential first step toward a clear, stress-free fertility journey. Dr. Kamran Saleem provides unhurried 45–60 minute consultations to review your blood test reports, answer your questions thoroughly, and design a tailored treatment plan without pressure for unnecessary procedures.</p>
  <a class="btn" href={wa}>Book on WhatsApp</a>
  <div class="cards c3 locs">
    {locations.map(([n, a, h, l]) => <a class="card link" href={l}><h3>{n}</h3><p>{a}</p><p class="hrs">{h}</p></a>)}
  </div>
  <p style="margin-top:22px"><a style="color:#fff" href={S}>All assessment services</a> · <a style="color:#fff" href={T}>Fertility treatment</a> · <a style="color:#fff" href="/services/support">Second opinions</a></p>
</div></section>
</main>
</div>
</Layout>

<style is:global>
